@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy & Data Protection";
}

<article class="content privacy-page" aria-labelledby="privacyTitle">
    <div class="eyebrow">PRIVACY &amp; DATA PROTECTION</div>
    <h1 id="privacyTitle">Privacy &amp; Data Protection</h1>
    <p class="privacy-intro">
        SafeRoute AI is designed to help users make more informed travel decisions by providing route information and road-safety insights.
    </p>

    <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="informationCollectedTitle">
        <h2 id="informationCollectedTitle">Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>
            The application may collect information such as account details, journey locations and community incident reports when users interact with its features.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="informationUseTitle">
        <h2 id="informationUseTitle">How Information Is Used</h2>
        <p>
            Information is intended to support route planning, road-safety assessments, community reporting and improvements to the application.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="locationInformationTitle">
        <h2 id="locationInformationTitle">Location Information</h2>
        <p>
            Location details may be used to identify journey starting points, destinations and reported road incidents.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="dataProtectionTitle">
        <h2 id="dataProtectionTitle">Data Protection</h2>
        <p>
            SafeRoute AI aims to handle user information responsibly and protect personal information. Access to information will be governed by the security measures implemented in the application.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section" aria-labelledby="privacyNoticeTitle">
        <h2 id="privacyNoticeTitle">Privacy Notice</h2>
        <p>
            SafeRoute AI is currently under development. The collection, storage, processing and handling of information will depend on the final system implementation and applicable data-protection requirements.
        </p>
    </section>
</article>